# D-Bus activation for push-to-talk capture (PLAN §5.7.5).
#
# Same executable and the same unit as dev.lisaos.Overlay1: one process
# owns both names. It still needs its own file, because activation is
# per-NAME — without it the first key press finds nobody on
# dev.lisaos.Voice1 and voice only works when something else happened to
# start the backend first, which is the kind of bug that reproduces for
# nobody.
#
# `SystemdService=` names the same unit deliberately: systemd starts
# lisa-overlayd.service and waits for its BusName=dev.lisaos.Overlay1,
# and the process claims Voice1 in the same run. See #294 for why a
# bare `Exec=` here was a process outside every sandbox and outside the
# egress gate's population.
[D-BUS Service]
Name=dev.lisaos.Voice1
Exec=/usr/bin/lisa-app overlay-extension/backend/lisa-overlayd.js
SystemdService=lisa-overlayd.service
